{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794173001,"nonce":"HOIQ7SKSD3Q0pGyZq0k0mrXSnNU=","title":"A value Jira removed is archived in the schema, always","message":"Found in a real Jira sync: Jira dropped statuses from workflows. Derive only warned `dead alias: Jira has no value N here any more` and left the value live, so a local write could still set a status Jira cannot hold. The values were removed by hand with a schema import.\n\n## Design\n\n- Derive archives a value whose Jira alias is dead every time, whether or not issues hold it.\n- An archived value is a per-value state in the schema, the counterpart of `schema archive` on a type or field. If no per-value archive exists yet, this task adds it. An archived value:\n  - stays readable: issues holding it read, `--at` history replays, `issue log` shows it;\n  - is refused on every new write, through the same schema check, naming the values the field accepts;\n  - is left out of pickers and of anything that offers values to choose.\n- The note derive prints names the issues that still hold the archived value, because someone has to decide what happens to them.\n- `doc/design/schema.md` gains the archived value, `doc/design/jira.md` the derive rule, and the quickstart's schema section the archived value if it changes how the schema is used.\n\n## Test\n\n- Drop a status from the fake Jira workflow: derive archives it, an issue holding it still reads, a `set` to it is refused, and the note lists that issue.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["issue-model","bridge"],"parent":"8ade81134de7c2f5d1a16c3a48efc761b35bbf4cc2a58eaf8189fa5c15621e01","priority":"high","status":"to-do","type":"task"}}]}